.TH UPTIME 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
uptime \- tell how long the computer has been running
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B uptime
.RB [ \-p ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B uptime
prints how long the computer has been running since it booted, as
procps's uptime does:
.PP
.nf
 up 5 min
 up  1:05
 up 2 days,  1:05
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-pretty
Says it in words:
.BR "up 1 hour, 5 minutes" .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0; 1, with a usage message, for any other argument.
.SH NOTES
mcos has no real-time clock, so there is no time of day; and no load
average or user count either. The uptime is the machine's own clock, which
stands still while its chunk is unloaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR time (1)
